{"title":"ATA read/write sectors","slug":"ATA_read_write_sectors","html":"<p>Since interrupts (like INT 13h) can't be called easily in protected mode or long mode, direct disk access through ports might be the only solution. The below code is example of subroutines to read and write disk sectors directly from the first hard disk (80h) in long mode using CHS and LBA.</p>\n<h2 id=\"ata_read_sectors\">ATA read sectors</h2>\n<h3 id=\"read_in_chs_mode\">Read in CHS mode</h3>\n<p>Accessing disk using CHS (cylinder,head,sector) indexes seem to be kinda old type but is the base for LBA access. The following NASM long-mode subroutine reads CH sectors to memory address indicated by RDI register.</p>\n<div class=\"sourceCode\" id=\"cb1\"><pre class=\"sourceCode nasm\"><code class=\"sourceCode nasm\"><span id=\"cb1-1\"><span class=\"co\">;=============================================================================</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-2\"><span class=\"co\">; ATA read sectors (CHS mode) </span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-3\"><span class=\"co\">; Max head index is 15, giving 16 possible heads</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-4\"><span class=\"co\">; Max cylinder index can be a very large number (up to 65535)</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-5\"><span class=\"co\">; Sector is usually always 1-63, sector 0 reserved, max 255 sectors/track</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-6\"><span class=\"co\">; If using 63 sectors/track, max disk size = 31.5GB</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-7\"><span class=\"co\">; If using 255 sectors/track, max disk size = 127.5GB</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-8\"><span class=\"co\">; See OSDev forum links in bottom of [http://wiki.osdev.org/ATA]</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-9\"><span class=\"co\">;</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-10\"><span class=\"co\">; @param EBX The CHS values; 2 bytes, 1 byte (BH), 1 byte (BL) accordingly</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-11\"><span class=\"co\">; @param CH The number of sectors to read</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-12\"><span class=\"co\">; @param RDI The address of buffer to put data obtained from disk               </span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-13\"><span class=\"co\">;</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-14\"><span class=\"co\">; @return None</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-15\"><span class=\"co\">;=============================================================================</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-16\"><span class=\"fu\">ata_chs_read:</span>   <span class=\"kw\">pushfq</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-17\">                <span class=\"kw\">push</span> <span class=\"kw\">rax</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-18\">                <span class=\"kw\">push</span> <span class=\"kw\">rbx</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-19\">                <span class=\"kw\">push</span> <span class=\"kw\">rcx</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-20\">                <span class=\"kw\">push</span> <span class=\"kw\">rdx</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-21\">                <span class=\"kw\">push</span> <span class=\"kw\">rdi</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-22\">                </span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-23\">                <span class=\"kw\">mov</span> <span class=\"kw\">rdx</span><span class=\"op\">,</span><span class=\"bn\">1f6h</span>            <span class=\"co\">;port to send drive &amp; head numbers</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-24\">                <span class=\"kw\">mov</span> <span class=\"kw\">al</span><span class=\"op\">,</span><span class=\"kw\">bh</span>               <span class=\"co\">;head index in BH</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-25\">                <span class=\"kw\">and</span> <span class=\"kw\">al</span><span class=\"op\">,</span><span class=\"bn\">00001111b</span>        <span class=\"co\">;head is only 4 bits long</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-26\">                <span class=\"kw\">or</span>  <span class=\"kw\">al</span><span class=\"op\">,</span><span class=\"bn\">10100000b</span>        <span class=\"co\">;default 1010b in high nibble</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-27\">                <span class=\"kw\">out</span> <span class=\"kw\">dx</span><span class=\"op\">,</span><span class=\"kw\">al</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-28\"></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-29\">                <span class=\"kw\">mov</span> <span class=\"kw\">rdx</span><span class=\"op\">,</span><span class=\"bn\">1f2h</span>            <span class=\"co\">;Sector count port</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-30\">                <span class=\"kw\">mov</span> <span class=\"kw\">al</span><span class=\"op\">,</span><span class=\"kw\">ch</span>               <span class=\"co\">;Read CH sectors</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-31\">                <span class=\"kw\">out</span> <span class=\"kw\">dx</span><span class=\"op\">,</span><span class=\"kw\">al</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-32\"></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-33\">                <span class=\"kw\">mov</span> <span class=\"kw\">rdx</span><span class=\"op\">,</span><span class=\"bn\">1f3h</span>            <span class=\"co\">;Sector number port</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-34\">                <span class=\"kw\">mov</span> <span class=\"kw\">al</span><span class=\"op\">,</span><span class=\"kw\">bl</span>               <span class=\"co\">;BL is sector index</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-35\">                <span class=\"kw\">out</span> <span class=\"kw\">dx</span><span class=\"op\">,</span><span class=\"kw\">al</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-36\"></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-37\">                <span class=\"kw\">mov</span> <span class=\"kw\">rdx</span><span class=\"op\">,</span><span class=\"bn\">1f4h</span>            <span class=\"co\">;Cylinder low port</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-38\">                <span class=\"kw\">mov</span> <span class=\"kw\">eax</span><span class=\"op\">,</span><span class=\"kw\">ebx</span>             <span class=\"co\">;byte 2 in ebx, just above BH</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-39\">                <span class=\"kw\">mov</span> <span class=\"kw\">cl</span><span class=\"op\">,</span><span class=\"dv\">16</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-40\">                <span class=\"kw\">shr</span> <span class=\"kw\">eax</span><span class=\"op\">,</span><span class=\"kw\">cl</span>              <span class=\"co\">;shift down to AL</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-41\">                <span class=\"kw\">out</span> <span class=\"kw\">dx</span><span class=\"op\">,</span><span class=\"kw\">al</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-42\"></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-43\">                <span class=\"kw\">mov</span> <span class=\"kw\">rdx</span><span class=\"op\">,</span><span class=\"bn\">1f5h</span>            <span class=\"co\">;Cylinder high port</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-44\">                <span class=\"kw\">mov</span> <span class=\"kw\">eax</span><span class=\"op\">,</span><span class=\"kw\">ebx</span>             <span class=\"co\">;byte 3 in ebx, just above byte 2</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-45\">                <span class=\"kw\">mov</span> <span class=\"kw\">cl</span><span class=\"op\">,</span><span class=\"dv\">24</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-46\">                <span class=\"kw\">shr</span> <span class=\"kw\">eax</span><span class=\"op\">,</span><span class=\"kw\">cl</span>              <span class=\"co\">;shift down to AL</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-47\">                <span class=\"kw\">out</span> <span class=\"kw\">dx</span><span class=\"op\">,</span><span class=\"kw\">al</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-48\"></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-49\">                <span class=\"kw\">mov</span> <span class=\"kw\">rdx</span><span class=\"op\">,</span><span class=\"bn\">1f7h</span>            <span class=\"co\">;Command port</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-50\">                <span class=\"kw\">mov</span> <span class=\"kw\">al</span><span class=\"op\">,</span><span class=\"bn\">20h</span>              <span class=\"co\">;Read with retry.</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-51\">                <span class=\"kw\">out</span> <span class=\"kw\">dx</span><span class=\"op\">,</span><span class=\"kw\">al</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-52\">                </span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-53\"><span class=\"fu\">.still_going:</span>   <span class=\"kw\">in</span> <span class=\"kw\">al</span><span class=\"op\">,</span><span class=\"kw\">dx</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-54\">                <span class=\"kw\">test</span> <span class=\"kw\">al</span><span class=\"op\">,</span><span class=\"dv\">8</span>               <span class=\"co\">;the sector buffer requires servicing.</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-55\">                <span class=\"cf\">jz</span> <span class=\"fu\">.still_going</span>         <span class=\"co\">;until the sector buffer is ready.</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-56\"></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-57\">                <span class=\"kw\">mov</span> <span class=\"kw\">rax</span><span class=\"op\">,</span><span class=\"dv\">512</span><span class=\"op\">/</span><span class=\"dv\">2</span>           <span class=\"co\">;to read 256 words = 1 sector</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-58\">                <span class=\"kw\">xor</span> <span class=\"kw\">bx</span><span class=\"op\">,</span><span class=\"kw\">bx</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-59\">                <span class=\"kw\">mov</span> <span class=\"kw\">bl</span><span class=\"op\">,</span><span class=\"kw\">ch</span>               <span class=\"co\">;read CH sectors</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-60\">                <span class=\"kw\">mul</span> <span class=\"kw\">bx</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-61\">                <span class=\"kw\">mov</span> <span class=\"kw\">rcx</span><span class=\"op\">,</span><span class=\"kw\">rax</span>             <span class=\"co\">;RCX is counter for INSW</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-62\">                <span class=\"kw\">mov</span> <span class=\"kw\">rdx</span><span class=\"op\">,</span><span class=\"bn\">1f0h</span>            <span class=\"co\">;Data port, in and out</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-63\">                <span class=\"kw\">rep</span> insw                <span class=\"co\">;in to [RDI]</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-64\"></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-65\">                <span class=\"kw\">pop</span> <span class=\"kw\">rdi</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-66\">                <span class=\"kw\">pop</span> <span class=\"kw\">rdx</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-67\">                <span class=\"kw\">pop</span> <span class=\"kw\">rcx</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-68\">                <span class=\"kw\">pop</span> <span class=\"kw\">rbx</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-69\">                <span class=\"kw\">pop</span> <span class=\"kw\">rax</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-70\">                <span class=\"kw\">popfq</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb1-71\">                <span class=\"cf\">ret</span></span></code></pre></div>\n<h3 id=\"read_in_lba_mode\">Read in LBA mode</h3>\n<div class=\"wk-note wk-stub\">\n<p><span class=\"wk-note-label\">Stub</span></p>\n<p>This page on the OSDev Wiki is a stub: it covers the basics but is not complete.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"sourceCode\" id=\"cb2\"><pre class=\"sourceCode nasm\"><code class=\"sourceCode nasm\"><span id=\"cb2-1\"><span class=\"co\">;=============================================================================</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb2-2\"><span class=\"co\">; ATA read sectors (LBA mode) </span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb2-3\"><span class=\"co\">;</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb2-4\"><span class=\"co\">; @param EAX Logical Block Address of sector</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb2-5\"><span class=\"co\">; @param CL  Number of sectors to read</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb2-6\"><span class=\"co\">; @param RDI The address of buffer to put data obtained from disk</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb2-7\"><span class=\"co\">;</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb2-8\"><span class=\"co\">; @return None</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb2-9\"><span class=\"co\">;=============================================================================</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb2-10\"><span class=\"fu\">ata_lba_read:</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb2-11\">               <span class=\"kw\">pushfq</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb2-12\">               <span class=\"kw\">and</span> <span class=\"kw\">rax</span><span class=\"op\">,</span> <span class=\"bn\">0x0FFFFFFF</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb2-13\">               <span class=\"kw\">push</span> <span class=\"kw\">rax</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb2-14\">               <span class=\"kw\">push</span> <span class=\"kw\">rbx</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb2-15\">               <span class=\"kw\">push</span> <span class=\"kw\">rcx</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb2-16\">               <span class=\"kw\">push</span> <span class=\"kw\">rdx</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb2-17\">               <span class=\"kw\">push</span> <span class=\"kw\">rdi</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb2-18\"></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb2-19\">               <span class=\"kw\">mov</span> <span class=\"kw\">rbx</span><span class=\"op\">,</span> <span class=\"kw\">rax</span>         <span class=\"co\">; Save LBA in RBX</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb2-20\">               </span>\r\n<span id=\"cb2-21\">               <span class=\"kw\">mov</span> <span class=\"kw\">edx</span><span class=\"op\">,</span> <span class=\"bn\">0x01F6</span>      <span class=\"co\">; Port to send drive and bit 24 - 27 of LBA</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb2-22\">               <span class=\"kw\">shr</span> <span class=\"kw\">eax</span><span class=\"op\">,</span> <span class=\"dv\">24</span>          <span class=\"co\">; Get bit 24 - 27 in al</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb2-23\">               <span class=\"kw\">or</span> <span class=\"kw\">al</span><span class=\"op\">,</span> <span class=\"bn\">11100000b</span>     <span class=\"co\">; Set bit 6 in al for LBA mode</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb2-24\">               <span class=\"kw\">out</span> <span class=\"kw\">dx</span><span class=\"op\">,</span> <span class=\"kw\">al</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb2-25\"></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb2-26\">               <span class=\"kw\">mov</span> <span class=\"kw\">edx</span><span class=\"op\">,</span> <span class=\"bn\">0x01F2</span>      <span class=\"co\">; Port to send number of sectors</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb2-27\">               <span class=\"kw\">mov</span> <span class=\"kw\">al</span><span class=\"op\">,</span> <span class=\"kw\">cl</span>           <span class=\"co\">; Get number of sectors from CL</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb2-28\">               <span class=\"kw\">out</span> <span class=\"kw\">dx</span><span class=\"op\">,</span> <span class=\"kw\">al</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb2-29\">               </span>\r\n<span id=\"cb2-30\">               <span class=\"kw\">mov</span> <span class=\"kw\">edx</span><span class=\"op\">,</span> <span class=\"bn\">0x1F3</span>       <span class=\"co\">; Port to send bit 0 - 7 of LBA</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb2-31\">               <span class=\"kw\">mov</span> <span class=\"kw\">eax</span><span class=\"op\">,</span> <span class=\"kw\">ebx</span>         <span class=\"co\">; Get LBA from EBX</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb2-32\">               <span class=\"kw\">out</span> <span class=\"kw\">dx</span><span class=\"op\">,</span> <span class=\"kw\">al</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb2-33\"></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb2-34\">               <span class=\"kw\">mov</span> <span class=\"kw\">edx</span><span class=\"op\">,</span> <span class=\"bn\">0x1F4</span>       <span class=\"co\">; Port to send bit 8 - 15 of LBA</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb2-35\">               <span class=\"kw\">mov</span> <span class=\"kw\">eax</span><span class=\"op\">,</span> <span class=\"kw\">ebx</span>         <span class=\"co\">; Get LBA from EBX</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb2-36\">               <span class=\"kw\">shr</span> <span class=\"kw\">eax</span><span class=\"op\">,</span> <span class=\"dv\">8</span>           <span class=\"co\">; Get bit 8 - 15 in AL</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb2-37\">               <span class=\"kw\">out</span> <span class=\"kw\">dx</span><span class=\"op\">,</span> <span class=\"kw\">al</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb2-38\"></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb2-39\"></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb2-40\">               <span class=\"kw\">mov</span> <span class=\"kw\">edx</span><span class=\"op\">,</span> <span class=\"bn\">0x1F5</span>       <span class=\"co\">; Port to send bit 16 - 23 of LBA</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb2-41\">               <span class=\"kw\">mov</span> <span class=\"kw\">eax</span><span class=\"op\">,</span> <span class=\"kw\">ebx</span>         <span class=\"co\">; Get LBA from EBX</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb2-42\">               <span class=\"kw\">shr</span> <span class=\"kw\">eax</span><span class=\"op\">,</span> <span class=\"dv\">16</span>          <span class=\"co\">; Get bit 16 - 23 in AL</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb2-43\">               <span class=\"kw\">out</span> <span class=\"kw\">dx</span><span class=\"op\">,</span> <span class=\"kw\">al</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb2-44\"></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb2-45\">               <span class=\"kw\">mov</span> <span class=\"kw\">edx</span><span class=\"op\">,</span> <span class=\"bn\">0x1F7</span>       <span class=\"co\">; Command port</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb2-46\">               <span class=\"kw\">mov</span> <span class=\"kw\">al</span><span class=\"op\">,</span> <span class=\"bn\">0x20</span>         <span class=\"co\">; Read with retry.</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb2-47\">               <span class=\"kw\">out</span> <span class=\"kw\">dx</span><span class=\"op\">,</span> <span class=\"kw\">al</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb2-48\"></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb2-49\"><span class=\"fu\">.still_going:</span>  <span class=\"kw\">in</span> <span class=\"kw\">al</span><span class=\"op\">,</span> <span class=\"kw\">dx</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb2-50\">               <span class=\"kw\">test</span> <span class=\"kw\">al</span><span class=\"op\">,</span> <span class=\"dv\">8</span>           <span class=\"co\">; the sector buffer requires servicing.</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb2-51\">               <span class=\"cf\">jz</span> <span class=\"fu\">.still_going</span>      <span class=\"co\">; until the sector buffer is ready.</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb2-52\"></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb2-53\">               <span class=\"kw\">mov</span> <span class=\"kw\">rax</span><span class=\"op\">,</span> <span class=\"dv\">256</span>         <span class=\"co\">; to read 256 words = 1 sector</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb2-54\">               <span class=\"kw\">xor</span> <span class=\"kw\">bx</span><span class=\"op\">,</span> <span class=\"kw\">bx</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb2-55\">               <span class=\"kw\">mov</span> <span class=\"kw\">bl</span><span class=\"op\">,</span> <span class=\"kw\">cl</span>           <span class=\"co\">; read CL sectors</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb2-56\">               <span class=\"kw\">mul</span> <span class=\"kw\">bx</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb2-57\">               <span class=\"kw\">mov</span> <span class=\"kw\">rcx</span><span class=\"op\">,</span> <span class=\"kw\">rax</span>         <span class=\"co\">; RCX is counter for INSW</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb2-58\">               <span class=\"kw\">mov</span> <span class=\"kw\">rdx</span><span class=\"op\">,</span> <span class=\"bn\">0x1F0</span>       <span class=\"co\">; Data port, in and out</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb2-59\">               <span class=\"kw\">rep</span> insw             <span class=\"co\">; in to [RDI]</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb2-60\"></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb2-61\">               <span class=\"kw\">pop</span> <span class=\"kw\">rdi</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb2-62\">               <span class=\"kw\">pop</span> <span class=\"kw\">rdx</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb2-63\">               <span class=\"kw\">pop</span> <span class=\"kw\">rcx</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb2-64\">               <span class=\"kw\">pop</span> <span class=\"kw\">rbx</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb2-65\">               <span class=\"kw\">pop</span> <span class=\"kw\">rax</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb2-66\">               <span class=\"kw\">popfq</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb2-67\">               <span class=\"cf\">ret</span></span></code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"ata_write_sectors\">ATA write sectors</h2>\n<p>A write is mostly equivalent to performing a read operation. The only changes needed are a change in command (0x30 for chs write), and the direction of the data, which is written (rep outsw from *SI) to the data port rather than read (rep insw to *DI).</p>\n<div class=\"sourceCode\" id=\"cb3\"><pre class=\"sourceCode nasm\"><code class=\"sourceCode nasm\"><span id=\"cb3-1\"><span class=\"co\">;=============================================================================</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb3-2\"><span class=\"co\">; ATA write sectors (LBA mode) </span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb3-3\"><span class=\"co\">;</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb3-4\"><span class=\"co\">; @param EAX Logical Block Address of sector</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb3-5\"><span class=\"co\">; @param CL  Number of sectors to write</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb3-6\"><span class=\"co\">; @param RDI The address of data to write to the disk</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb3-7\"><span class=\"co\">;</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb3-8\"><span class=\"co\">; @return None</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb3-9\"><span class=\"co\">;=============================================================================</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb3-10\"></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb3-11\"><span class=\"fu\">ata_lba_write:</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb3-12\">    <span class=\"kw\">pushfq</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb3-13\">    <span class=\"kw\">and</span> <span class=\"kw\">rax</span><span class=\"op\">,</span> <span class=\"bn\">0x0FFFFFFF</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb3-14\">    <span class=\"kw\">push</span> <span class=\"kw\">rax</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb3-15\">    <span class=\"kw\">push</span> <span class=\"kw\">rbx</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb3-16\">    <span class=\"kw\">push</span> <span class=\"kw\">rcx</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb3-17\">    <span class=\"kw\">push</span> <span class=\"kw\">rdx</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb3-18\">    <span class=\"kw\">push</span> <span class=\"kw\">rdi</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb3-19\">    </span>\r\n<span id=\"cb3-20\">    <span class=\"kw\">mov</span> <span class=\"kw\">rbx</span><span class=\"op\">,</span> <span class=\"kw\">rax</span>         <span class=\"co\">; Save LBA in RBX</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb3-21\"></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb3-22\">    <span class=\"kw\">mov</span> <span class=\"kw\">edx</span><span class=\"op\">,</span> <span class=\"bn\">0x01F6</span>      <span class=\"co\">; Port to send drive and bit 24 - 27 of LBA</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb3-23\">    <span class=\"kw\">shr</span> <span class=\"kw\">eax</span><span class=\"op\">,</span> <span class=\"dv\">24</span>          <span class=\"co\">; Get bit 24 - 27 in al</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb3-24\">    <span class=\"kw\">or</span> <span class=\"kw\">al</span><span class=\"op\">,</span> <span class=\"bn\">11100000b</span>     <span class=\"co\">; Set bit 6 in al for LBA mode</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb3-25\">    <span class=\"kw\">out</span> <span class=\"kw\">dx</span><span class=\"op\">,</span> <span class=\"kw\">al</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb3-26\"></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb3-27\">    <span class=\"kw\">mov</span> <span class=\"kw\">edx</span><span class=\"op\">,</span> <span class=\"bn\">0x01F2</span>      <span class=\"co\">; Port to send number of sectors</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb3-28\">    <span class=\"kw\">mov</span> <span class=\"kw\">al</span><span class=\"op\">,</span> <span class=\"kw\">cl</span>           <span class=\"co\">; Get number of sectors from CL</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb3-29\">    <span class=\"kw\">out</span> <span class=\"kw\">dx</span><span class=\"op\">,</span> <span class=\"kw\">al</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb3-30\"></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb3-31\">    <span class=\"kw\">mov</span> <span class=\"kw\">edx</span><span class=\"op\">,</span> <span class=\"bn\">0x1F3</span>       <span class=\"co\">; Port to send bit 0 - 7 of LBA</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb3-32\">    <span class=\"kw\">mov</span> <span class=\"kw\">eax</span><span class=\"op\">,</span> <span class=\"kw\">ebx</span>         <span class=\"co\">; Get LBA from EBX</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb3-33\">    <span class=\"kw\">out</span> <span class=\"kw\">dx</span><span class=\"op\">,</span> <span class=\"kw\">al</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb3-34\"></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb3-35\">    <span class=\"kw\">mov</span> <span class=\"kw\">edx</span><span class=\"op\">,</span> <span class=\"bn\">0x1F4</span>       <span class=\"co\">; Port to send bit 8 - 15 of LBA</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb3-36\">    <span class=\"kw\">mov</span> <span class=\"kw\">eax</span><span class=\"op\">,</span> <span class=\"kw\">ebx</span>         <span class=\"co\">; Get LBA from EBX</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb3-37\">    <span class=\"kw\">shr</span> <span class=\"kw\">eax</span><span class=\"op\">,</span> <span class=\"dv\">8</span>           <span class=\"co\">; Get bit 8 - 15 in AL</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb3-38\">    <span class=\"kw\">out</span> <span class=\"kw\">dx</span><span class=\"op\">,</span> <span class=\"kw\">al</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb3-39\"></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb3-40\"></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb3-41\">    <span class=\"kw\">mov</span> <span class=\"kw\">edx</span><span class=\"op\">,</span> <span class=\"bn\">0x1F5</span>       <span class=\"co\">; Port to send bit 16 - 23 of LBA</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb3-42\">    <span class=\"kw\">mov</span> <span class=\"kw\">eax</span><span class=\"op\">,</span> <span class=\"kw\">ebx</span>         <span class=\"co\">; Get LBA from EBX</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb3-43\">    <span class=\"kw\">shr</span> <span class=\"kw\">eax</span><span class=\"op\">,</span> <span class=\"dv\">16</span>          <span class=\"co\">; Get bit 16 - 23 in AL</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb3-44\">    <span class=\"kw\">out</span> <span class=\"kw\">dx</span><span class=\"op\">,</span> <span class=\"kw\">al</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb3-45\"></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb3-46\">    <span class=\"kw\">mov</span> <span class=\"kw\">edx</span><span class=\"op\">,</span> <span class=\"bn\">0x1F7</span>       <span class=\"co\">; Command port</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb3-47\">    <span class=\"kw\">mov</span> <span class=\"kw\">al</span><span class=\"op\">,</span> <span class=\"bn\">0x30</span>         <span class=\"co\">; Write with retry.</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb3-48\">    <span class=\"kw\">out</span> <span class=\"kw\">dx</span><span class=\"op\">,</span> <span class=\"kw\">al</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb3-49\"></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb3-50\"><span class=\"fu\">.still_going:</span>  <span class=\"kw\">in</span> <span class=\"kw\">al</span><span class=\"op\">,</span> <span class=\"kw\">dx</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb3-51\">    <span class=\"kw\">test</span> <span class=\"kw\">al</span><span class=\"op\">,</span> <span class=\"dv\">8</span>           <span class=\"co\">; the sector buffer requires servicing.</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb3-52\">    <span class=\"cf\">jz</span> <span class=\"fu\">.still_going</span>      <span class=\"co\">; until the sector buffer is ready.</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb3-53\"></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb3-54\">    <span class=\"kw\">mov</span> <span class=\"kw\">rax</span><span class=\"op\">,</span> <span class=\"dv\">256</span>         <span class=\"co\">; to read 256 words = 1 sector</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb3-55\">    <span class=\"kw\">xor</span> <span class=\"kw\">bx</span><span class=\"op\">,</span> <span class=\"kw\">bx</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb3-56\">    <span class=\"kw\">mov</span> <span class=\"kw\">bl</span><span class=\"op\">,</span> <span class=\"kw\">cl</span>           <span class=\"co\">; write CL sectors</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb3-57\">    <span class=\"kw\">mul</span> <span class=\"kw\">bx</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb3-58\">    <span class=\"kw\">mov</span> <span class=\"kw\">rcx</span><span class=\"op\">,</span> <span class=\"kw\">rax</span>         <span class=\"co\">; RCX is counter for OUTSW</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb3-59\">    <span class=\"kw\">mov</span> <span class=\"kw\">rdx</span><span class=\"op\">,</span> <span class=\"bn\">0x1F0</span>       <span class=\"co\">; Data port, in and out</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb3-60\">    <span class=\"kw\">mov</span> <span class=\"kw\">rsi</span><span class=\"op\">,</span> <span class=\"kw\">rdi</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb3-61\">    <span class=\"kw\">rep</span> outsw            <span class=\"co\">; out</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb3-62\"></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb3-63\">    <span class=\"kw\">pop</span> <span class=\"kw\">rdi</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb3-64\">    <span class=\"kw\">pop</span> <span class=\"kw\">rdx</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb3-65\">    <span class=\"kw\">pop</span> <span class=\"kw\">rcx</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb3-66\">    <span class=\"kw\">pop</span> <span class=\"kw\">rbx</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb3-67\">    <span class=\"kw\">pop</span> <span class=\"kw\">rax</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb3-68\">    <span class=\"kw\">popfq</span></span>\r\n<span id=\"cb3-69\">    <span class=\"cf\">ret</span></span></code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"see_also\">See also</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a class=\"ext\" href=\"http://forum.osdev.org/viewtopic.php?t=12268\" rel=\"noopener\">Read/write disk sectors by Dex</a></li>\n<li><a data-wiki=\"ATA PIO Mode\" href=\"#/library/ATA_PIO_Mode\">ATA PIO mode</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"ext wk-missing\" href=\"https://wiki.osdev.org/ATA\" rel=\"noopener\">ATA</a></li>\n</ul>\n","toc":[{"id":"ata_read_sectors","text":"ATA read sectors","level":2},{"id":"read_in_chs_mode","text":"Read in CHS mode","level":3},{"id":"read_in_lba_mode","text":"Read in LBA mode","level":3},{"id":"ata_write_sectors","text":"ATA write sectors","level":2},{"id":"see_also","text":"See also","level":2}],"categories":["ATA"],"rating":null,"flags":["stub"],"words":1251,"summary":"Since interrupts (like INT 13h) can't be called easily in protected mode or long mode, direct disk access through ports might be the only solution. The below code is example of subroutines to read and write disk sectors…","updated":"2017-04-19","authors":["A22347"],"url":"https://wiki.osdev.org/ATA_read/write_sectors","history":"https://wiki.osdev.org/index.php?title=ATA_read/write_sectors&action=history","backlinks":[],"lessons":[{"id":"t9m2l3","title":"ATA PIO: your first disk driver","kind":"further"}]}